# This file exists for JaCoCo's benefit, not as cosmetic Lombok configuration (quick task
# 260812-eg8). Lombok's generated members (getters/setters/builders/equals/hashCode/etc.) are
# NOT a separate compiled artifact JaCoCo can exclude by path or class-file pattern -- they are
# inline members woven into the same .class file as the hand-written code around them. JaCoCo
# has had a built-in filter for members carrying the standard `@lombok.Generated` annotation
# since 0.8.2, but that filter only fires when Lombok actually stamps the annotation, which it
# does NOT do by default. Without this file, every entity's and DTO's Lombok-generated
# accessors, builder, equals/hashCode would count against the coverage denominator this task's
# whole job is to measure honestly (design_rationale, trade-off 1) -- systematically deflating
# the real, hand-written-code coverage number underneath every class this repo has annotated
# with @Getter/@Setter/@Builder/@EqualsAndHashCode.
#
# This repository had no lombok.config at all before this quick task.
lombok.addLombokGeneratedAnnotation = true

# Makes this file authoritative at the repo root: without stopBubbling, Lombok would keep
# searching parent directories for another lombok.config and could merge in unrelated settings
# from outside this project (e.g. a machine-wide config a contributor happens to have).
config.stopBubbling = true
